; `calc on` decides whether a number is in a set that a theory binds to the calculator: natural.kurt
; `calc Nat naturals`, number.kurt `calc Int integers` and `calc Rat rationals`, and
; set.kurt `calc in element`
load natural
calc on
3 ∈ Nat
0 ∈ Nat
-3 ∈ Int
1 / 3 ∈ Rat
0.25 ∈ Rat
expect "ProofError"
    -3 ∈ Nat
expect "ProofError"
    1 / 3 ∈ Int
expect "ProofError"
    x ∈ Nat
3 + 4 ∈ Nat
calc off
